\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Persistence classes of a retained trace}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{Fix a trace record #{T} from \ref{ftip-00P5} and a declared receipt
interface with event indicators #{e_{\rm term}(t)}, #{e_{\rm ev}(t)},
#{e_{\rm pass}(t)},
#{e_{\rm fail}(t)}, #{e_{\rm rec}(t)} and a productive-novelty indicator
#{n_{\rm prod}(t)} for #{0\leq t\leq H}. Let #{u(t)} be the declared task-value
score and #{u^{\rm sat}} its saturation threshold. The source's reported
horizon tradeoff and selective refinement
\citet{Sections 5.2 and 6-7; Tables 4-5, 10}{dang2026selecting} motivate
these observable classes, which are an FTIP proposal. Write}
##{
\tau_{\rm end}:=\inf\{t:e_{\rm term}(t)=1\},\quad
\tau_{\rm ev}:=\inf\{t:e_{\rm ev}(t)=1\},\quad
\tau_{\rm pass}:=\inf\{t:e_{\rm pass}(t)=1\},
}
##{
\tau_{\rm fail}:=\inf\{t:e_{\rm fail}(t)=1\},\quad
\tau_{\rm rec}:=\inf\{t:e_{\rm rec}(t)=1\},\quad
\tau_{\rm sat}:=\inf\{t:u(t)\geq u^{\rm sat}\},
}
\p{with #{\inf\varnothing:=+\infty}. The receipt declares all indicators and
the score as functions of the same run, so the following classes are
replayable predicates rather than impressions about an agent's inner state.}
##{
\operatorname{Prem}(T):=\mathbf 1[\tau_{\rm end}<\tau_{\rm ev}\lor
(\tau_{\rm fail}<\tau_{\rm end}\land\tau_{\rm rec}\geq\tau_{\rm end})],
}
##{
\operatorname{Prod}(T):=\mathbf 1[\tau_{\rm ev}<\tau_{\rm end}\land
\tau_{\rm pass}<\tau_{\rm end}\land
(\tau_{\rm fail}\geq\tau_{\rm end}\lor
\tau_{\rm fail}<\tau_{\rm rec}<\tau_{\rm end})],
}
##{
\operatorname{Over}(T):=\mathbf 1[\tau_{\rm sat}<\tau_{\rm end}\land
\sum_{t=\tau_{\rm sat}}^{\tau_{\rm end}-1}n_{\rm prod}(t)=0].
}
\p{A productive trace reaches evidence and a final verifier pass, and any
failure before termination is followed by recovery. An over-persistent trace
continues after saturation without another declared productive event. The
experiment may refine #{n_{\rm prod}} for a task family, but it must declare
that predicate before comparing selectors.}
